' Bug 4: a Select Case branch with a multi-value list and an EMPTY body
' (nothing between it and the next Case) fails to compile, but with a
' confusing, misattributed error message.
'
' How to see the bug:
'   1. Compile this file with the CURRENT (unfixed) compiler.
'   2. Compilation fails with:  Invalid variable name: 13,10
'      attributed to the "Case Else" line below - even though nothing on
'      that line is a variable name. The real issue is the empty-bodied
'      "Case 13, 10" line just above it.
'   3. This is a COMPILE-time failure - the program never builds, so there
'      is no LCD output to see for this one; the chip/LCD setup below is
'      only present for consistency with the sibling test file and to keep
'      this a realistic, complete program once the bug is fixed.
'
' Expected/correct behaviour once fixed: this should compile cleanly, with
' Case 13, 10 acting as a no-op (falls straight through to End Select) for
' either of those two values, and the LCD should show "OK" underneath.

#chip 16f877a, 20
'Setup LCD Parameters (4-bit bus, matches Vendor_Boards\Real_Pic_Simulator\LCD_demonstration.gcb)
#DEFINE LCD_IO 4
#DEFINE LCD_NO_RW
#DEFINE LCD_SPEED FAST

#DEFINE LCD_RS PortB.4
#DEFINE LCD_Enable PortB.5
#DEFINE LCD_DB4 PortB.0
#DEFINE LCD_DB5 PortB.1
#DEFINE LCD_DB6 PortB.2
#DEFINE LCD_DB7 PortB.3

#option explicit

Dim MyByte As Byte
MyByte = 13

CLS
Print "SELECT CASE BUG"
Locate 1,0
Print "EMPTY CASE BODY"
Wait 3 s

CLS
Locate 0,0
Print "TEST (13,10):"
Locate 1,0

Select Case MyByte
  Case 13, 10
    ' <<< deliberately empty - this is what triggers the bug
  Case Else
    Print "UNEXPECTED"
End Select

Print "OK"                 ' <<< only reached once this compiles and falls through correctly

Do
Loop
